<title>CHILE: RESEARCH ALERT - Madeco upgraded to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Madeco upgraded to hold.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Santander Investment raised its rating on shares of Chilean copper industrial company Manufacturas de Cobre SA (Madeco) to hold from underperform.</p>
<p>-- Santander analyst Catalina Le Blanc said the share price has fallen 20 percent since the underperform rating on July 17.</p>
<p>-- Madeco should achieve 13.2 percent compound annual growth in operating income in the three years from 1996 to 1999, the firm said.</p>
<p>- Revised earnings estimates are attractive.</p>
<p>- 12-month price target is $26 per ADR.</p>
<p>- The stock rose 2.2 percent to 945 pesos.</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
</text>
